# Peer whitelist for the Apothem (testnet) node.
#
# When this file lists at least one enode, start-apothem.sh restricts the node
# to these peers only:
#   - every enode is added as a static and trusted peer (always dialed, never
#     dropped for peer limits),
#   - peer discovery is disabled (--nodiscover),
#   - only the listed node IDs are accepted (--peers-allowlist); any other
#     peer is rejected right after the handshake, before it can trigger a sync.
#
# The hub node listed here must set PEER_WHITELIST_HUB=true in .env: it keeps
# discovery off but skips the allowlist so the other nodes can connect to it.
# Put the node IDs of peers still on the old chain in PEER_DENYLIST on the hub.
#
# Leave the file without enodes (comments only) to keep normal peer discovery.
# Set PEER_WHITELIST=false in .env to ignore this file.
#
# One enode per line, IPv4 address and port, e.g.
# enode://<128 hex node id>@1.2.3.4:30312
# Get a node's enode with ./enode.sh on that host.

# Hub: DK04_XF_MasterNode (0x1a1b58d133effb6ba1631da7297d8cd58f65fa73), at block 83599999
enode://b3e242c2346557e8b4f7378bf17e0ad020046cd5e41be8e46d0148bfbd85cd36a9e3813f0bd7f34fcf6d5cd4d11bd375864f8d03aeaabb15d308238f2e55e4cb@38.143.58.165:30313
